WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.380
The edge springs are used to ensure
that your edge stitches knit correctly.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.080
Although knitters say that they've

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:13.040
successfully knit without using them,
to prevent misformed stitches and possible

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:18.180
jamming, it's best to get in the habit
of positioning them while you're knitting.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.300
The edge spring has a rounded ridge

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.500
that fits into the rounded
slot on the needle bed.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:27.040
The edge spring slips along the needle bed

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:32.060
and is aligned with the outer
edge needles the knitting.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.140
The latch of the edge
needle must be closed.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:40.240
The best way to ensure this is
to position the edge spring.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.460
Push the latch needle out so
the latch moves past the edge spring.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:52.180
Pull the needle back and the edge spring
will close the latch automatically.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.280
Position the needle with the edge of the
needle channel and you're ready to knit.

